# Regime Recall Run Flowchart

Entry point: [`tests/test_regime_recall.py`](/home/dooces/Projects/dreth/tests/test_regime_recall.py)

Run modes:

```bash
python3 tests/test_regime_recall.py           # canonical verbose receipt run, then stress sweep
python3 tests/test_regime_recall.py --stress  # stress sweep only
```

Canonical parameters are defined in the test file: `seed=3`, `n_vars=35`,
`n_stable=800`, `probe_top_k=1`, `n_recover=600`. The harness does not enter
through `dreth_causal_v28.py`, `cli.run`, `--mode v29`, or `dreth_extensions`.
It constructs the world and agent directly, then installs a v30 forms bundle.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([tests/test_regime_recall.py __main__]) --> B{--stress in argv?}
    B -- no --> R[run_receipt(SEED, N_VARS, N_STABLE, verbose=True)]
    B -- yes --> S[run_stress()]
    R --> S

    subgraph RECEIPT["run_receipt(seed, n_vars, n_stable, probe_top_k, n_recover)"]
        direction TB
        R0[make_agent] --> R0a[CausalWorld(n_vars, rng_w)]
        R0a --> R0b[ChainedAgent(world, rng_a)]
        R0b --> R0c[agent.probe_retention_per_var = 0]
        R0c --> R0d[V30Bundle(enable_forms=True,\nform_discovery_every=50,\nform_min_instances=2,\nform_probe_top_k=probe_top_k)]
        R0d --> R0e[agent.initialize]
        R0e --> WARM[run_n(world, agent, n_stable, start=1)]

        subgraph WARMUP["warm-up loop"]
            direction TB
            W0[world.perturb_by_schedule(c, shaped)] --> W1{mutation.kind == REVEAL?}
            W1 -- yes --> W2[agent.on_variable_revealed]
            W1 -- no --> W3[agent.run_cycle]
            W3 --> V30[v30.on_cycle_start]
            V30 --> DISC{cycle - last_discovery_cycle >= 50?}
            DISC -- yes --> FORMS[_run_form_discovery]
            DISC -- no --> CYCLE[normal agent cycle continues]
        end

        FORMS --> F1[discover_forms\nregister/rebind shared operator+arity forms]
        F1 --> F2[discover_form_compressions]
        F2 --> F3[discover_form_sentinels\npopulate sentinel_template]
        F3 --> F4[propagate_form_compressions]
        F4 --> F5[increment strong_observations]
        F5 --> F6[update_co_occurrence\nactive form pairs += 1\nticks_active += 1]
        F6 --> F7[evaluate_form_health]

        WARM --> PICK[discover_forms(reg)\nchoose HIGH_CO_ID and ALT_ID]
        PICK --> P0{valid pair?}
        P0 -- no --> SKIP[return SKIP]
        P0 -- yes --> CHECK[norm_high > norm_alt?]
        CHECK -- no --> FAIL[return FAIL]
        CHECK -- yes --> R1

        subgraph R1["Receipt 1: quarantine + probe recovery"]
            direction TB
            Q1[force_quarantine(HIGH_CO_ID, n_stable + 1)] --> C1[cycles_to_reactivate]
            C1 --> C1a[per cycle: perturb schedule]
            C1a --> C1b[agent.run_cycle or on_variable_revealed]
            C1b --> H1[evaluate_form_health probes quarantined/probation form]
            H1 --> H2[probe_quarantined_form\nsentinel_template probes via\nworld.predict_var_under_intervention]
            H2 --> H3{hit_rate >= 0.6?}
            H3 -- quarantined --> H4[health_status = probation\nprobation_passes = 1]
            H3 -- probation --> H5[probation_passes += 1]
            H5 --> H6{probation_passes >= 2?}
            H6 -- yes --> H7[health_status = active\nlog REACTIVATED via probe]
            H3 -- fail --> H8[probe_fail_count += 1\nor probation resets to quarantined]
        end

        R1 --> R23

        subgraph R23["Receipts 2 and 3: cascade recall + A* ordering"]
            direction TB
            R20[make fresh world2/agent2] --> R21[run warm-up again]
            R21 --> R22[discover HIGH_CO_ID2, ALT_ID2]
            R22 --> R23a[force_quarantine both forms]
            R23a --> R24[snapshot_agent(agent2)\nfor flat selector comparison]
            R24 --> ASTAR[cycles_to_reactivate on agent2\nusing select_probe_candidates]
            R24 --> FLAT[monkeypatch forms_module.select_probe_candidates = _flat_select\ncycles_to_reactivate on snapshot]
            ASTAR --> ASEL[A* priority:\nco_score + same-shape match*5 + dormancy - fail*2 + warm bonus]
            FLAT --> FSEL[flat priority:\ninsertion order only]
            ASEL --> CASCADE{HIGH_CO reactivated?}
            CASCADE -- yes --> CQ[queue top quarantined/probation co-occurrence neighbors\nin _warm_probe_queue\nlog queued for recall probe]
            FSEL --> COMPARE[compare cycles and interventions]
            CQ --> COMPARE
        end

        COMPARE --> SUMMARY[return PASS, PARTIAL, SKIP, or FAIL result dict]
    end

    subgraph STRESS["run_stress()"]
        direction TB
        S0[iterate STRESS_GRID] --> S1[run_receipt(..., verbose=False)]
        S1 --> S2[print status table]
        S2 --> S3{any FAIL?}
        S3 -- yes --> S4[raise SystemExit]
        S3 -- no --> S5[finish]
    end

    style A fill:#1a1a2e,color:#e0e0e0
    style RECEIPT fill:#080808,color:#e0e0e0
    style WARMUP fill:#111111,color:#e0e0e0
    style FORMS fill:#001a1a,color:#e0e0e0
    style F7 fill:#001a0a,color:#e0e0e0
    style R1 fill:#0d1a0d,color:#e0e0e0
    style R23 fill:#1a1a00,color:#e0e0e0
    style STRESS fill:#0d0d0d,color:#e0e0e0
```

## What The Test Proves

| Receipt | Setup | Passing evidence |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Probe recovery** | The dynamically selected `HIGH_CO_ID` form is force-quarantined after warm-up. | `cycles_to_reactivate` observes the form become `active`, and the form health log contains `REACTIVATED via probe`. Recovery uses `probe_quarantined_form`, which resolves `sentinel_template` probes through form bindings and calls `world.predict_var_under_intervention`. |
| **2. Cascade recall** | A fresh agent is warmed up; `HIGH_CO_ID2` and `ALT_ID2` are both force-quarantined. | After `HIGH_CO_ID2` reactivates, `evaluate_form_health` queues co-occurrence neighbors in `_warm_probe_queue` and writes `queued for recall probe` to `agent2.ledger.event_log`. If ordering passes but no cascade event fires, the harness returns `PARTIAL`, not `FAIL`. |
| **3. A* priority ordering** | The same quarantined pair is run twice: normal A* selection on `agent2`, and flat insertion-order selection on a deep-copied snapshot. | A* being slower than flat returns `PARTIAL` (heuristic suboptimal for this parameter set); `FAIL` is reserved for R1 failures only. A* slower is an efficiency signal, not a correctness failure. |

`HIGH_CO_ID` and `ALT_ID` are not hardcoded by the executable logic. The test
selects them with [`discover_forms`](/home/dooces/Projects/dreth/tests/test_regime_recall.py:193):
both forms must be eligible 2-ary forms, directly co-occur, and the high form
must have a larger form id but a higher normalized co-occurrence score than the
alternate. This creates the A* vs flat contrast.

Normalized co-occurrence is:

```text
sum(raw_co(form, active_peer) / max(1, min(form.ticks_active, active_peer.ticks_active)))
```

The sum can exceed `1.0` because multiple active peers can contribute.

