## Hot Path During Warm-Up And Recovery

Inside `agent.run_cycle`, the receipt still exercises the normal agent loop:
v30 maintenance at cycle start, topological order, cheap-path checks, full
audits up to the priority budget, install/certify, and final cycle accounting.
The receipt is narrower than the old single-run CLI chart, though: cold storage,
NN proposers, `dreth_extensions`, CLI argument parsing, and `--mode v29` are not
part of this entry path.

The expensive per-variable work remains the same when a full audit is needed:
`_full_audit_var` calls `fit_var`, which enumerates hypotheses, chooses
interventions, and scores hypotheses with the NumPy batched scorer. New fits
flow through `_install_var`, where sentinels and any compressions are installed.

## Receipt Constants

The test docstring records the expected canonical discovery shape for the
current seed and parameters:

| Form | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `FORM_0009` | Expected high co-occurrence form for the canonical run. It has a larger id than the alternate, so flat insertion order deprioritizes it. |
| `FORM_0002` | Expected alternate form for the canonical run. It has a smaller id, so flat selection chooses it first. |
| `FORM_0007`, `FORM_0010` | Expected active peer forms that help provide the co-occurrence signal. |

Treat those as canonical expectations, not as fixed harness inputs. The harness
uses the dynamic selector above so stress runs can report `PASS`, `PARTIAL`,
`SKIP`, or `FAIL` based on each parameter set.

